{
    "chapter_num": 8,
    "verses_count": 18,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "David’s Further Conquests"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "After this it came to pass that David "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. struck"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "attacked the Philistines and subdued them. And David took "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. The Bridle of the Mother City"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Metheg Ammah from the hand of the Philistines."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he defeated Moab. Forcing them down to the ground, he measured them off with a line. With two lines he measured off those to be put to death, and with one full line those to be kept alive. So the Moabites became David’s servants, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " brought tribute."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "David also defeated Hadadezer the son of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to recover his territory at the River Euphrates. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "David took from him one thousand "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "chariots,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "seven thousand, 1 Chr. 18:4"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "seven hundred horsemen, and twenty thousand foot soldiers. Also David hamstrung all the chariot "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "horses"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ", except that he spared "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "enough"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of them for one hundred chariots."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah, David killed twenty-two thousand of the Syrians. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus; and the Syrians became David’s servants, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " brought tribute. So the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " preserved David wherever he went. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And David took the shields of gold that had belonged to the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Also from "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Tibhath, 1 Chr. 18:8"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Betah and from Berothai,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Chun, 1 Chr. 18:8"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " cities of Hadadezer, King David took a large amount of bronze."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Tou, 1 Chr. 18:9"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Toi king of Hamath heard that David had defeated all the army of Hadadezer, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "then Toi sent "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Hadoram, 1 Chr. 18:10"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Joram his son to King David, to "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. ask him of his welfare"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "greet him and bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer and defeated him (for Hadadezer had been at war with Toi); and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "Joram"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " brought with him articles of silver, articles of gold, and articles of bronze. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "King David also dedicated these to the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ", along with the silver and gold that he had dedicated from all the nations which he had subdued— "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "from "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "LXX, Syr., Heb. mss. Edom"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Syria, from Moab, from the people of Ammon, from the Philistines, from Amalek, and from the spoil of Hadadezer the son of Rehob, king of Zobah."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And David made "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "himself"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " a name when he returned from killing eighteen thousand "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "LXX, Syr., Heb. mss. Edomites and 1 Chr. 18:12"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Syrians in the Valley of Salt. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He also put garrisons in Edom; throughout all Edom he put garrisons, and all the Edomites became David’s servants. And the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " preserved David wherever he went."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "David’s Administration"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So David reigned over all Israel; and David administered judgment and justice to all his people. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Joab the son of Zeruiah "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " over the army; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " recorder; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Zadok the son of Ahitub and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the priests; "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Shavsha, 1 Chr. 18:16"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Seraiah "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "secretary"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "scribe; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Benaiah the son of Jehoiada "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was over"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " both the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and David’s sons were "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. priests"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "chief ministers."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}